<headroom-library version="1" id="clean-bakersfield-twang" category="Clean" order="50" instrument="guitar" style="Country">
  <description>Hard, bright West Coast country twang: a loud high-powered blackface twin with the bright switch on and treble and mids up, no compressor, a short slap and a little of the amp's own spring. Bridge pickup, played near the bridge with a thin pick; turn the guitar down to tame it rather than the amp.</description>
  <tags><tag>Clean</tag><tag>Country</tag><tag>Twang</tag><tag>Slapback</tag><tag>Spring Reverb</tag></tags>
  <sources>
    <source url="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Don_Rich" title="Don Rich (Wikipedia)"/>
    <source url="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bakersfield_sound" title="Bakersfield sound (Wikipedia)"/>
    <source url="https://www.fender.com/articles/instruments/buck-owens-and-the-silver-sparkle" title="Fender: Buck Owens and the silver sparkle"/>
    <source url="https://www.tdpri.com/threads/don-rich-buckaroos-tone.582787/" title="TDPRI: Don Rich / Buckaroos tone (incl. Jerry Brightman's account)"/>
  </sources>
</headroom-library>
</headroom-preset>
